# Commits and pull requests

Commit **only when the user asks**. Before every commit, run `npm run lint` and **fix failures** (do not `--no-verify` unless the user explicitly asks). Prefer `npm run typecheck` as well when `src/` or tests change.

## Conventional commits

Format: `type(optional-scope): short summary`

Use the **type** that matches the change. Scope is optional (`track`, `roadmap`, `auth`, `ci`).

| Type | When |
| --- | --- |
| `feat` | User-facing behavior that did not exist before |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `docs` | Docs, ADRs, Cursor rules only |
| `style` | Formatting; no logic change |
| `refactor` | Restructure without changing behavior |
| `perf` | Performance |
| `test` | Tests only |
| `chore` | Tooling, deps, housekeeping |
| `ci` | GitHub Actions / workflow config |
| `build` | Build or bundler config |
| `revert` | Revert a previous commit (`revert: feat(track): …`) |

Subject: imperative, ~72 chars, no trailing period. Body (optional): why, not a file list.

Examples: `feat(track): persist chat per role`, `fix(roadmap): refresh notes after Track accept`, `docs: add deployment runbook`.

## `[skip ci]`

CI on `main` and PRs runs lint, typecheck, tests, migration check, build, and Playwright (see `.github/workflows/ci.yml`). GitHub skips that workflow when the commit message contains `[skip ci]` or `[ci skip]`.

**Prefer `[skip ci]`** when the diff cannot affect the app or CI itself, for example:

- Markdown / ADRs / `docs/`
- `.cursor/rules/`
- Comments or copy with no runtime impact

Put it at the end of the subject or on its own body line: `docs: add deployment runbook [skip ci]`.

**Do not skip CI** when anything in `src/`, tests, `supabase/migrations/`, `package.json` / lockfile, Playwright, Next config, or `.github/workflows/` changed. If unsure, run CI.

## Pull requests

Title uses the same conventional type as the commits (or the primary type if mixed). Body: short summary and a test plan. Do not force-push `main`. Use `gh pr create` when the user asks for a PR.
